# One line-ending policy, on every platform.
#
# The built bundles in lib/ are committed as LF and their sha256 is recorded in
# notes/harness.md. On a machine with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) git
# materializes those files as CRLF, so a rebuild that writes LF left `git status`
# reporting the tree dirty although the blobs were byte-identical — and the recorded
# hashes stopped describing the bytes a Windows checkout actually had on disk.
* text=auto eol=lf
